From: openRuyi Project Contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve any in empty generic constraint diagnostics

Go 1.27 prints the underlying empty interface as interface{}, whereas older
toolchains could print any. Stripping the interface braces leaves an empty
constraint description. Normalize empty constraints to any explicitly so
diagnostics retain the constraint and existing exact assertions still hold.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Upstream: https://github.com/butuzov/ireturn

diff --git a/analyzer/analyzer.go b/analyzer/analyzer.go
--- a/analyzer/analyzer.go
+++ b/analyzer/analyzer.go
@@ -178,6 +178,9 @@ func filterInterfaces(p *analysis.Pass, ft *ast.FuncType, di map[string]struct{}
 				if strings.HasSuffix(typeParams, suffix) {
 					typeParams = typeParams[:len(typeParams)-1]
 				}
+				if isEmpty {
+					typeParams = "any"
+				}
 
 				// todo: write test for this (1.18&1.19 only?)
 				goVersion := runtime.Version()
